  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/6359c29b-4b03-4bca-8c6d-7bf1bcb624ec.png\" style=\"width: 350px; height: 176px;\"/></p><p>Both diodes are in forward bias. In forward bias, potential drop across <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>G</mi><mi>e</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></math> will be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo> </mo><mo>&amp;</mo><mo> </mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>7</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> respectively.</p><p>Therefore, current in the circuit <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>15</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>1000</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo> </mo><mi>mA</mi></math></p><p>Required potential drop across <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></math>, <br/><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi><msub><mi>R</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>×</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>1000</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>75</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo> </mo></math></p></blockquote>",
